prompt.text:
Repair the complete CommonJS source below and return a corrected complete source file exporting exactly `{ selectBuildPages }`.

`selectBuildPages(manifest, requested)` selects independent pages for a partial build. `manifest` contains records `{ slug, revision, content }`, where `slug` and `content` are strings and `revision` is a non-negative safe integer. Slugs must be non-empty and unique. `requested` must contain unique, non-empty strings, each present in the manifest. Shape failures throw `TypeError`; duplicates and missing requested slugs throw `RangeError`.

Return selected records in requested order. Every returned record must be a fresh object so modifying it cannot affect the manifest. Do not mutate either input. Empty inputs produce an empty result, while a non-empty request against an empty manifest reports a missing slug.

Known-bad source:
```javascript
function selectBuildPages(manifest, requested) {
  if (!Array.isArray(manifest) || !Array.isArray(requested)) throw new TypeError('Inputs must be arrays');
  const bySlug = new Map();
  for (const page of manifest) {
    if (!page || typeof page !== 'object' || typeof page.slug !== 'string' || page.slug.length === 0 ||
        typeof page.content !== 'string' || !Number.isSafeInteger(page.revision) || page.revision < 0) {
      throw new TypeError('Invalid page');
    }
    if (bySlug.has(page.slug)) throw new RangeError('Duplicate manifest slug');
    bySlug.set(page.slug, page);
  }
  const seen = new Set();
  return requested.map((slug) => {
    if (typeof slug !== 'string' || slug.length === 0) throw new TypeError('Invalid requested slug');
    if (seen.has(slug)) throw new RangeError('Duplicate requested slug');
    seen.add(slug);
    const page = bySlug.get(slug);
    if (!page) throw new RangeError('Requested slug is missing');
    return page;
  });
}

module.exports = { selectBuildPages };
```

